ght division. The other medalist was losing semi-finalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/142492"} "Enmanuel Reyes"] " of Spain."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The 2023 World Champion and silver medalist from Tokyo, " [:a {:href "/athletes/146228"} "Muslim Gadzhimagomedov"] " (ROC), was barred from competing because of his nationality. Cuba’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/123514"} "Julio César la Cruz"] ", the reigning champion from the previous two Games, lost to Azerbaijani Loren Alfonso, a Cuban by birth, by a split 3-2 decision in round two, one judge having la Cruz as winning all three rounds of the bout."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/151160"} "Lazizbek Mullojonov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/UZB"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/UZB.png"}] "UZB"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/140915"} "Loren Alfonso"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AZE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AZE.png"}] "AZE"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/151139"} "Davlat Boltaev"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/TJK"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/TJK.png"}] "TJK"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/142492"} "Enmanuel Reyes"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ESP"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-cent